{
  "title": "SQLite pilot bench still models the Postgres all-versions trigram indexes",
  "description": "scripts/sqlite-pilot-bench.py builds its own Postgres schema (PG_SCHEMA / PG_INDEXES) instead of running the migrations, so it still creates the trigram indexes over every recipe_versions row and pg_search has no is_current predicate. \
Migration 2026-10-15-000000-0000_current_version_search_indexes made the real indexes partial on is_current (kept in step by a trigger on recipes.current_version_id), so the bench's Postgres search numbers in doc/sqlite-pilot-analysis.md overstate today's cost. \
Add is_current to the bench schema (set during COPY and on the bench's repoint writes), make the indexes partial, add the predicate to pg_search, and rerun the bench to refresh the doc's search comparison.",
